# PERF-POOL-1T experiments — 2026-06-10 (/goal hunt, closure-attribution lead)
#
# Finding that motivated this: dwarf+disasm attribution resolved the two
# hot LocalKey::with symbols (8.3% + 7.0% on terminal e7 at --threads 1)
# to rayon Registry::in_worker_cold + LockLatch StackJobs — the
# out-of-pool main thread cold-bridging every internal parallel_map /
# par_sort into the AMBIENT global pool. KEY REALIZATION: `--threads 1`
# has never meant sequential internals; run_with_threads(1) direct-calls
# the encode body and its par-iters fan out to the default-width pool.
#
# Experiment 1 — true one-worker pool at threads<=1 (install):
#   terminal +149%  imac_dark +136%  noaa +195%  clic097 +71%  (REJECTED
#   — ambient-width parallelism dwarfs the bridge toll; .tsv alongside)
# Experiment 2 — warm entry via rayon::join (one cold bridge per encode):
#   terminal +2.22%  imac_dark +1.65%  noaa -1.32%  clic097 +3.67%
#   (REJECTED — hosting the body on a worker loses more than the
#   per-call bridges cost; perf_pool1t_warm_2026-06-10.tsv)
